        ['q' => 'How is this score calculated?', 'a' => 'Every question is a five-point scale from -2 (Not at all) to +2 (Absolutely). One question doesn\'t feed just one trait — the same question counts toward several traits, each with its own weight, and weights can be negative (reverse-scored: answering "Absolutely" subtracts). A trait\'s percentage = Σ(your answer × weight) ÷ Σ(2 × |weight|); a negative result is recorded as 0, because "nothing like it" should read 0%, not 50%. The denominator is that trait\'s own maximum, so every trait is measured against its own ceiling — how many questions feed a trait doesn\'t affect fairness, only resolution. The four spectrums accumulate independently and, divided by their question counts, convert to a -8 to +8 scale. This is also why the 20 percentages don\'t add up to 100%: each one means "how much you\'re like this type," not a share. The "how is this score calculated" section at the bottom of every result page also lists how many questions measure that type, which sections they span, and how many are reverse-scored. The weight table lives only on the server and is never sent to the browser.'],
